# AI Agent Instruction - Source of Truth

All agents contributing to this project MUST follow the SDLC protocol: **THINK -> PLAN -> CODE**.
Before making any changes or planning new features, read the documentation files in the `docs/` folder:

1. `docs/AGENT_GUIDELINES.md` - Core operating rules for AI agents
2. `docs/PRD.md` - Product requirements and functional scope
3. `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` - System architecture and directory organization
4. `docs/DATABASE_SCHEMA.md` - Database schema, indexes, and future-proofing
5. `docs/DESIGN_TOKENS_AND_UI.md` - UI design tokens, colors, and components
6. `docs/NAMING_CONVENTIONS.md` - Naming conventions and code standards
7. `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` - Frontend & backend best practices
8. `docs/TASKS.md` - Task roadmap and tracking

Always maintain the documentation as the single source of truth. If any architectural or schema change occurs, update the relevant docs immediately.
